Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:31:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] candidate: 5.7.16.1 test build with SnapAlloc 34-int fallback
 (MR !44464)

Same Mesa lock (69f1f21) and patch set as 5.7.15.1, plus
upstream-mr44464-snapalloc-34ints.patch: the u_gralloc fallback reads the
UBWC flag of SnapAlloc display-core handles (34 ints per view, Snapdragon
8 Elite generation) when the handle has exactly that shape and its stride
matches the gralloc stride; every other handle keeps
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID. The MR's 33-int SM7435 branch is not included.

A840 evidence: with identical settings, 5.7.14.1 shows column noise and
the 5.7.14.1 + MR !44464 lab renders clean (Rick confirmed the whole
session). Hardware for this candidate (A840, A740 regression), CTS and
VVL are not-run.

